From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gpl: -cluster_pull_weight pulls rtl_macro_placer's clusters
 together

rtl_macro_placer -keep_clustering_data writes its clusters into the
database as VISUAL_DEBUG groups, which global placement ignores. With
-cluster_pull_weight w, Nesterov placement pulls each cluster's cells
(every group under the root) toward the cluster's area-weighted
centroid. The force on a cell is bounded by w, like w pins, and grows
with distance inside the cluster's packed radius; it fades linearly to
0 at iteration -cluster_pull_iters (150), after which placement is the
stock code path. A pull that never fades fights density spreading and
diverges; DG-RePlAce decays its virtual-net weights for the same reason.

The pull enters the summed gradient only, not the wirelength gradient,
so the initial density penalty and the reported wirelength are those
without it. Cells are mapped to clusters serially, in cell order, on
every gradient update, so the result is the same at any thread count.
With the weight at 0 nothing is computed and placement is unchanged.

Carried in bazel-orfs to measure Hier-RTLMP clusters in global
placement (bazel-orfs #1263); not upstreamed. Retires when an upstream
gpl has a cluster or dataflow term, or when the measurement says no.
